  "editorial": {
    "status": "working-edition",
    "notes": "The commixture: the particle broken from the Host is let fall into the chalice, and the prayer names what has been done. COMMÍXTIO at w002 occurs once in the whole Ordo. ACCIPIÉNTIBUS at w013 is a present participle agreeing with nobis, which is dative with fiat: may it be, to us who receive it, unto eternal life. The Amen at w018 is the priest's own, said secretly with the rest, so it is kept in the same segment rather than set apart as a response.",
